data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_part.done","item_id":"rs_d1ed60f47298485d3b4ba768d06166f4132dfd8c441144a790","output_index":0,"part":{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Crafting a weekly plan**\n\nI need to plan the week in a concise way. I could start with something generic like \"Mon–Fri: 9–11 deep work on Priority A and 11–12 for meetings.\" I'm considering stating that \"Tue/Thu are for admin and emails, while Wednesday is for review and planning.\" But wait, I need to make sure it really is one line! I’ll finalize it as: \"Mon–Fri: 9–11 deep work on Priority A, 11–12 meetings; 1–4 admin; Wed: review; Fri: wrap-up; Sat/Sun: rest.\""},"sequence_number":124,"summary_index":0}

